Reason: Random_setSeed rebuilt WELL512's sixteen state words but kept its position in them, so the same seed gave up to
16 different sequences depending on how many numbers had been drawn before. AM2R's randomizer seeds with the player's
custom seed and shuffles the items: the same seed came out as a different layout (11 of 20 runs differed). A seed now
gives the same sequence every time, so the same custom seed gives the same layout on every Wii. It is not GameMaker's
own seeding, so a seed probably still differs from the PC game's layout.
Upstream: Engine bug on every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

diff --git a/src/random.c b/src/random.c
--- a/src/random.c
+++ b/src/random.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include "random.h"
 
 void Random_setSeed(Random* m, uint32_t seed) {
+    m->index = 0;
     m->seed = seed;
     m->state[0] = seed;
     for (int i = 1; 16 > i; ++i)
